    "category": "network",
    "close_code": "Solved (Permanently)",
    "close_notes": "Regional analytics platform unreachable from the office - RESOLVED. Staff could not open a set of back-office tools from the corporate LAN, yet the same tools worked from home and for partners. The on-call first suspected a release that had shipped that day and nearly rolled it back. Before rolling back we checked the delivery path and the build - all healthy - so the release was NOT the cause. A maintenance window that night had consolidated the naming/resolution setup for that platform. Comparing the affected sub-zone against a healthy sibling sub-zone, and cross-checking each tool's live endpoint in the CMDB, we found the sibling delegated correctly to the corporate authoritative servers while the affected sub-zone delegated to servers that had been retired; a number of tools had lost their inside-the-network address entirely or had it pointing at a public or a decommissioned address; and several friendly-name aliases still chained to a retired name space. We restored each affected name to the live endpoint the CMDB listed, restored the delegation to the live authoritative servers the healthy sibling used, cleaned up the leftover aliases and a retired delegation, and left the public-facing entries and the genuinely public-only services alone. Access recovered. Lesson: verify the reported cause, compare against the healthy sibling and the CMDB, repair every affected name, and leave no leftover config. Closed.",
    "closed_at": "2026-05-09 16:10:00",
    "description": "A set of back-office tools was unreachable from the corporate LAN; a same-day release was suspected. See close notes.",
